# Lab BT Host (.108) — First Checks

When Phone↔Lab HU or Phone-role ESP↔real F20 fails (connect flaps, wrong name, “wird verwendet”, `failed to register accept channel 6`):

**Do not start with ESP OTA / RF theory.** Check `.108` host state first.

## Smoking guns (2026-11-19)

1. **Orphan alias pin:** `/tmp/bcl_dummy/alias_pin_persist.log` — abandoned `python3 -` can force **BMW 38304 on phone hci** forever.  
   `fuser -k /tmp/bcl_dummy/alias_pin_persist.log`
2. Other loops: `cod_pin_home.log`, `cod_pin_home_fast.log`, `phone87_hold.log` — Alias BMW↔Phone + car CoD on phone.
3. **Stale `hci_tcp_bridge`** after ESP reboot → `hci1 removed` / mid-connect drop. Restart bridges only after ESP `/api/status` ready.
4. BlueZ **Alias ≠ HCI Name**; only one powered **BMW 38304**.

## iDriveSim ↔ bt-analyzer resource conflict (Lösung)

**Konflikt:** Beide wollen RFCOMM **ch6** + BMW-Identität / Pair-Agent-Drop-Ins — nie parallel.

| Ressource | iDriveSim | bt-analyzer Lab (`f20_sim`) |
|-----------|-----------|------------------------------|
| RFCOMM ch6 | `idrivesim-rfcomm-bridge.service` (Unit oft auf **`.87`**) | `bcl_dummy_hu_agent.py hu --hu-profile f20_sim` |
| Pair-Agent | Drop-Ins `idrivesim-hu.conf` / `idrivesim-csr.conf` (BMW auf `.87` und/oder CSR) | `bmw-alias.conf` — BMW nur **`.131`**, `.87`=Phone |
| Symptom wenn falsch | Lab: `failed to register accept channel 6`; Phone sieht mehrere BMW / falschen Adapter | — |

**→ Lab (Phone → `.131` / f20_sim):**

```bash
systemctl stop idrivesim-rfcomm-bridge.service
pkill -f /opt/idrivesim/ || true
mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/bt-pair-agent.service.d.off
mv /etc/systemd/system/bt-pair-agent.service.d/idrivesim-*.conf \
   /etc/systemd/system/bt-pair-agent.service.d.off/ 2>/dev/null || true
systemctl daemon-reload
# dann nur .131 = BMW 38304 powered; ch6 frei für bcl_dummy_hu_agent
```

**→ iDriveSim:** `bcl_dummy_hu_agent` stoppen, `idrivesim-*.conf` zurück nach `service.d/`, `systemctl restart idrivesim-rfcomm-bridge bt-pair-agent`.

**Regel:** ch6 = idrivesim **xor** `bcl_dummy_hu_agent` — nie beide.

## Roles

| ESP | BD | Lab Phone→`.131` | Field Phone→F20 | iDriveSim (typ.) |
|-----|----|------------------|-----------------|------------------|
| `.131` | `…:7B:0A` | **HU / BMW 38304** | oft off | oft Phone (drop-in) |
| `.87` | `…:37:96` | Phone / off | **BT-Analyzer-Phone** → F20 | **HU** für rfcomm-bridge |

## B3 relay (Phone→.131 / .87→HU)

- Tool: `tools/b3_rfcomm_relay.py` (`rfcomm` + `--connect-adapter-bd`; `tcp-lab` for host-only).
- **No** .131↔.87 bond required: two independent ACLs; host copies ch6 bytes.
- BlueZ **Profile ch6 is host-global** — cannot run Profile HU + B3 listen both on ch6; lab air HU uses raw RFCOMM (`lab_b3_dual_esp_smoke.py`).
- Weak WiFi (~−80): Classic inquiry between D1s often fails — use existing bonds + `wifi_ps=none`; tcp-lab still validates decode.

